  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Systems Thinking for Sustainable Crime Prevention (2024), published by Taylor & Francis, has been cited 13 times — enough that OpenAlex puts it in the top 10% of works in its field and year. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 704 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Systems Thinking for Sustainable Crime Prevention by Vania Ceccato and Andy Newton was published by Taylor & Francis in 2024. Conceptually, the work connects to Crime prevention, Criminology, Political science, Environmental planning and Psychology.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 13 citations. That places it in the top 10% of works in its field and year of publication. Citations peaked in 2025 with 9 citing works. Notable citing venues include Sustainable development goals series, Valori e Valutazioni and Security Journal. The citing works include 6 journal articles, 4 book chapters and 1 review. They come from 8 countries, led by Sweden, Italy and Australia.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 704 times via OAPEN.</p>",
